# Preprojection State Taxonomy

The word "fixed point" is too broad for the distinctions now required.

## Exact-zero vacuum

```text
Phi(p)=0.
```

It is automatically critical for the squared-defect cost. Its Hessian is the
derivative Gram operator. It may have moduli or gauge zero modes and need not be
the unique vacuum.

## Nonzero-defect critical state

```text
Phi(p)!=0,
D Phi(p)^* Phi(p)=0.
```

The residual is invisible to every admissible infinitesimal repair direction at
that point. Stability depends on the full residual Hessian and on whether the
ambient or intrinsic admissible-stratum Hessian is intended.

## Sectorwise persistent defect

A connected or topological sector contains no exact zero. A coercive defect cost
therefore minimizes at positive value. This is a clean candidate for a
particle-like defect because persistence follows from the sector obstruction
rather than an inserted source term. The radial no-go requires the sector or
fixed-symbol restriction to be explicit.

## Symmetry orbit of equilibria

If the cost is invariant under a group, an equilibrium occurs as an orbit.
Orbit tangents are intrinsic Hessian zero modes. Stability is tested on the
reduced space or a normal slice.

## Relative equilibrium

The state moves only by a symmetry action:

```text
dC/dt = xi_M(C).
```

Its observables may be stationary even though the representative circulates.
This is distinct from a fixed point.

## Protected recurrent state

Reversible motion survives inside a null-dissipation sector. It can carry phase
or circulation while transverse directions repair. A strictly dissipative
gradient system cannot support this behavior.

## Constrained phase orbit

A normalized Clifford family can retain a full circle of first-order charges
with one constant square. Its tangent may look positive in the ambient Hessian
but is a zero mode of the intrinsic constrained Hessian after the second
fundamental term is included.

## Transient repair state

The cost decreases and the state approaches an invariant set. The repair
parameter is not automatically physical time.

## Stratified boundary state

The state lies on a singular support stratum. Linear tangent dynamics and
nonlinear normal costs must be kept separate; one ordinary global Hessian is
not available.
